    Input are two strings a and b consisting only of 1s and 0s.
    Perform binary XOR on these inputs and return result also as a string.
    >>> stringXor("010", "110")
    "100"
     */
    public String stringXor(String a, String b) {
        // Since the method is part of a utility-like class and might be used
        // in various contexts, we should ensure it's non-instantiable
        // But for this specific task, we just need to implement the XOR logic

        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();

        // Assuming both strings have the same length based on the example
        for (int i = 0; i < a.length(); i++) {
            char bitA = a.charAt(i);
            char bitB = b.charAt(i);

            // XOR logic: if bits are same, result is '0'; if different, result is '1'
            if (bitA == bitB) {
                result.append('0');
            } else {
                result.append('1');
            }
        }

        return result.toString();
    }
}

